  "knowledge_boundary_discovery_2603_21022": "KBD discovers an LLM's knowledge boundary with an RL policy rewarded by ENTROPY reduction. `worth(question)` here is the same quantity in the discrete case -- the number of operation verdicts one question decides -- so the ranking is measured rather than learned, with no policy and no parameters.",
  "llm_idea_2610_11253": "LLM-IDEA triages a plateau into capability limit / resolvable within the design class / certified exhausted, on the grounds that an agent which cannot tell 'not looked yet' from 'no further search will recover this' wastes its budget. That axis was ADDED here as `RESOLVABILITY`, decided per kind from evidence. The measured verdict on the current tree is that every unbound operation is rescuable and NONE is certified exhausted -- so no doubt in it is worth abandoning.",
  "skill_boundary_2026_03": "OSExpert-style exploration-then-execute reports +20% performance and 80% efficiency from exploring before acting -- and runs that loop inside a 120B model. The whole loop here is deterministic and costs 0 model calls; what it lacks is OSExpert's report, which this module now produces as a kind table."
 },
